## Hints for Future Agents
- stale-pr-note is a heuristic: sentences split on . ! ? followed by whitespace or end; the word "open" must match \bopen\b (case-insensitive), so "opened" and "reopen" do not fire; a PR is named by its full URL or by #<n> with an exact number match (#1550 is not #155).
- A number shared by several listed pull requests counts as open while any of them is OPEN or unknown; a literal URL mention is judged on that URL alone.
- Nothing calls gh without --github; the describe golden is unaffected because states is nil in that path.
- The note on 7b58c20 explains why states are never stored in the front matter.

## Codebase Discoveries
cmd.Output() with cmd.Stderr set to a builder still returns stdout and leaves stderr in the builder, which is how the reason line is captured.

